I look at my family.
"I am not alone here," I say.
"I have a friend."
My mother looks happy.
"A friend?" she asks.
"Yes," I say.
"Her name is Nina."
"She is my neighbour."
"And she is from Denmark."
My mother smiles.
"A Danish friend!"
"That is lovely, sweetheart," she says.
My father nods.
"That is good, Maya," he says.
My family is happy.
I am also happy because I have a friend here.
